# 130 - PRECEDENCE with a different KIND of answer if the ladder is wrong:
# rung 5 (+) binds tighter than rung 3 (==), so this is (1 + 2) == 3 and the
# answer is true. The wrong grouping, 1 + (2 == 3), is Int + Bool - a Type
# error, not a different Bool. There is no truthiness and no coercion (§6 .40),
# so a mis-ordered ladder cannot silently agree here.
--- source
print 1 + 2 == 3;
print "ab" + "c" == "abc";
--- expect
true
true
